        heading: "2. The Background Engine: Service Workers & The Ephemeral Lifecycle",
        paragraphs: [
          "The biggest mental shift in Manifest V3 is that **the background script is now an event-driven Service Worker (`background.service_worker`)**.",
          "Unlike MV2's persistent pages, a Service Worker has **no DOM** (`window`, `document`, and `Audio` do not exist). More importantly, its lifecycle is **ephemeral**: Chrome spawns the worker when an event fires, and automatically terminates it after **~30 seconds of inactivity** to free system memory.",
          "This ephemeral lifecycle completely breaks traditional JavaScript assumptions:",
          "• **No Global In-Memory State:** If you write `let activeCount = 0;` in your service worker, that variable will reset to `0` every time the worker wakes up from idle. All persistent state must be committed to `chrome.storage.local` or `chrome.storage.session`.",
          "• **No `setInterval` or `setTimeout`:** Long-running intervals will be killed midway when the worker goes dormant. In MV3, all scheduling must be handled via the **`chrome.alarms`** API, which wakes the service worker up reliably when the alarm fires.",
          "• **What if you really need a DOM?** If an extension needs to parse canvas graphics, decode audio, or inspect HTML strings, MV3 provides the **Offscreen Documents API** (`chrome.offscreen`), creating a headless HTML page on demand without reviving a permanent background page."
        ],
        codeLabel: "Service Worker Architecture: Handling Lifecycle & Event Listeners in MV3",
        code: `// background.js (MV3 Service Worker)

// ❌ ANTI-PATTERN: In-memory variables are wiped on idle termination!
// let cachedAuthToken = null;
// setInterval(() => checkStatus(), 60000); // ❌ Gets killed after 30s!

// ✅ BEST PRACTICE: Persist state with chrome.storage and schedule with chrome.alarms
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async () => {
  // Create an alarm for periodic background sync
  chrome.alarms.create("syncMilestones", { periodInMinutes: 15 });
  await chrome.storage.local.set({ extensionReady: true, lastRun: Date.now() });
});

// Alarm listener wakes the service worker automatically from dormant state
chrome.alarms.onAlarm.addListener(async (alarm) => {
  if (alarm.name === "syncMilestones") {
    const { extensionReady } = await chrome.storage.local.get("extensionReady");
    if (extensionReady) {
      console.log("[Worker] Woke up to process periodic maintenance!");
    }
  }
});

// One-time message listener from Content Scripts or Popups
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener((message, sender, sendResponse) => {
  if (message.type === "GET_CLIENT_DATA") {
    chrome.storage.local.get(["clientIndex"]).then((data) => {
      sendResponse({ status: "success", payload: data.clientIndex || [] });
    });
    return true; // Indicates async sendResponse
  }
});`
